<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA SELLS 6.62 BLN LEVS 1-WK DISCOUNT T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA SELLS 6.62 BLN LEVS 1-WK DISCOUNT T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on</p>
<p>Thursday sold 6,619 million levs of one-week discount T-bills,</p>
<p>yielding 3.73 percent to maturity, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The ministry approved all the bids that were received for a</p>
<p>total of 6.619 billion lev worth of T-bills.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3014097003</p>
<p> Term			    one week</p>
<p> Auction date		  February 6, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 6, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 February 13, 1997  Bids received    </p>
<p>	  6,619 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.40 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 6,619 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.40 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.73 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
